      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That is why they took the position that the August definition and the May definition were the same. That is why the district court took the position that the August definition and the May definitions were the same, because the district court agreed that that was what the definition of the class and the class of people who would have had standing, and perhaps, most importantly, that is why the Ninth Circuit resolved the question presented."
